<title>BRAZIL: FORECAST- Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are consensus forecasts from a survey of economic indicators taken from eight Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro brokerages and research firms. Also included are current market rates for dollar and interest rate futures over the next three months.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>*****Brazil Indicators - June Consensus Forecast***** --------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    INDICATOR	  PERIOD   AVG FORCST   MEDIAN     PRVS MONTH</p>
<p>CPI (Fipe)	  June    1.23   pct   1.26  pct  0.55     pct</p>
<p>PPI (IPA-M/FGV)   June    0.38   pct   0.40  pct  0.20     pct</p>
<p>Inflation (IGP-M) June    0.75   pct   0.70  pct  0.21     pct</p>
<p>Ind Act (IBGE)    May     3.31   pct   3.0   pct  3.50     pct</p>
<p>Trade Balance     June    -$405  million   -$385 million  -$271 million</p>
<p>Exports	     June    $4.651 bln   $4.65 bln  $4.658   bln</p>
<p>Imports	     June    $5.056 bln   $5.04 bln  $4.929   bln</p>
<p>				   ******</p>
<p>		Brazilian Financial Indicators</p>
<p>	   Futures market rates at June 23 close</p>
<p>			 June	     July	   August</p>
<p>Real/Dollar	   1.0782	   1.0862	 1.0943</p>
<p>Monthly Int Rates   1.601 pct	1.633 pct    1.639 pct</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Notes - Price indicators reflect monthly variation.</p>
<p>Industrial activity reflects annual variation.</p>
<p>((--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
